1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,574
Thank God, His people keep growing.

2
00:00:03,574 --> 00:00:07,439
Every Sunday, more families fill the church.

3
00:00:08,039 --> 00:00:12,748
But with so many faces, it becomes almost impossible to know who

4
00:00:12,748 --> 00:00:16,502
came, who is missing, and who quietly drifted away.

5
00:00:17,102 --> 00:00:18,634
Paper lists get lost.

6
00:00:18,634 --> 00:00:23,305
And the people who need a call the most are the easiest to miss.

7
00:00:23,905 --> 00:00:26,041
That's where Amoinee comes in.

8
00:00:26,041 --> 00:00:30,426
Amoinee, from the Coptic word for "Come!", helps every church

9
00:00:30,426 --> 00:00:33,588
know its people, and never lose one of them.

10
00:00:34,188 --> 00:00:38,618
For members, it starts with one simple step, done only once.

11
00:00:38,618 --> 00:00:43,018
Create your profile with your name and contact details, and

12
00:00:43,018 --> 00:00:46,002
choose whether to turn on face check-in.

13
00:00:46,002 --> 00:00:50,210
It's always your choice, and you can turn it off anytime.

14
00:00:50,810 --> 00:00:53,944
At the church door stands the Amoinee kiosk.

15
00:00:53,944 --> 00:00:56,722
Just look at the screen as you walk in.

16
00:00:56,722 --> 00:01:01,061
In a second it welcomes you by name, and records that you're

17
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:01,423
here.

18
00:01:02,023 --> 00:01:05,179
Prefer not to use your face? No problem.

19
00:01:05,179 --> 00:01:09,810
Scan the QR code on the kiosk with your phone, or type the

20
00:01:09,810 --> 00:01:12,045
three-digit code of the day.

21
00:01:12,045 --> 00:01:14,570
Nobody is ever left at the door.

22
00:01:15,170 --> 00:01:19,735
For Abouna and church servants, Amoinee turns attendance into

23
00:01:19,735 --> 00:01:20,109
care.

24
00:01:20,709 --> 00:01:25,573
The Today screen shows who is here, live, as the Liturgy begins,

25
00:01:25,573 --> 00:01:27,397
with every arrival time.

26
00:01:27,397 --> 00:01:31,820
Weekly events open check-in on their own, so no one has to

27
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:32,506
remember.

28
00:01:33,106 --> 00:01:37,049
The Members page keeps every person in one place, with their

29
00:01:37,049 --> 00:01:41,189
photo, consent status, and private notes that only the church's

30
00:01:41,189 --> 00:01:42,174
admins can see.

31
00:01:42,774 --> 00:01:46,676
And the Attendance Sheet gives Abouna a clear summary.

32
00:01:46,676 --> 00:01:51,272
How many came, who is faithful, who is drifting, and who hasn't

33
00:01:51,272 --> 00:01:54,263
come in weeks, ranked from most to least.

34
00:01:54,263 --> 00:01:58,808
A beautiful register shows every person at every service, at a

35
00:01:58,808 --> 00:01:59,321
glance.

36
00:02:09,374 --> 00:02:13,774
When someone misses several Sundays, Amoinee gently marks them

37
00:02:13,774 --> 00:02:15,122
"Follow up needed."

38
00:02:15,122 --> 00:02:19,676
Servants add labels like "Called," "Visited," "Needs prayer," or

39
00:02:19,676 --> 00:02:24,088
"Traveling," and can snooze a reminder when it's not the right

40
00:02:24,088 --> 00:02:24,444
time.

41
00:02:24,444 --> 00:02:28,847
Abouna also sees who came back, who is new, and whose birthday

42
00:02:28,847 --> 00:02:29,771
is this week.

43
00:02:30,371 --> 00:02:34,668
With one tap, Abouna can print a one-page report, or export

44
00:02:34,668 --> 00:02:36,124
everything to Excel.

45
00:02:36,124 --> 00:02:40,620
Each church sees only its own people, with access given church

46
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:44,898
by church, and privacy and consent built in from the start.

47
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:51,039
Because every soul matters, and no one should be forgotten.

48
00:02:51,039 --> 00:02:53,856
Amoinee. Come, let us worship.

